  "id": "tactile-encoding",
  "term": "tactile encoding",
  "definition": "Tactile encoding is the initial processing of a touch stimulus so it can be represented in space. In this source, it refers to the stage before later events such as an eye movement can update that tactile location into a gaze-dependent frame of reference.",
