      "reasons": [
        "The packet discusses tactile stimuli and a shift from gaze-independent to gaze-dependent reference frames contingent on when effector movement (gaze shift) occurs, but it does not explicitly define “tactile encoding” as the “initial processing of a touch stimulus” or state that it is processed “so it can be represented in space.”",
        "The definition’s claim that later events “such as an eye movement” update the tactile location is only supported indirectly (the packet refers to saccades/effector movement after tactile encoding), so the specific wording “eye movement can update that tactile location into a gaze-dependent frame of reference” is not directly stated as a definition-level claim in the packet."
